+# Focused security correction
+
+This patch removes secret activation scales from wire encoders, replaces the
+client mask generator with OS randomness and unbiased rejection, and removes
+the fixed default integrity challenge seed. It does not turn the protocol into
+maliciously secure inference. The share arithmetic remains a simulator. Its
+65537 field authenticates with roughly 16 bits, not the HE scheme's security
+level. Database rollback protection needs an external freshness anchor.
+
+The old scale field carries a constant one for compatibility. True scales remain
+local and still dequantize the exact same integer result. These changes do not
+change the quantized model. Existing sessions and preparation inventories should
+be discarded when changing to this build.
